   :message "Cache the parsed feed between runs

The importer parsed the whole feed on every run. It now keeps the
parsed records and reparses only what changed:
- Records are keyed by their source file and its modification time,
  so a touched file is reparsed even when its content is the same.
  - A deleted source file drops its records on the next run.
  - A renamed one counts as a deletion and an addition.
- The cache lives under `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/widgets`, and a version
  mismatch empties it.

The two options considered:
| Option            | Cold run | Warm run | Disk  |
| ----------------- | -------- | -------- | ----- |
| Reparse every run | 40 s     | 40 s     | 0     |
| Cache by mtime    | 41 s     | 3 s      | 80 MB |

Hashing contents instead of reading the modification time would cost
about as much as the parse it saves.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
